// examples/static_contracts.wll — v0.10 static contracts (spec §5.2 / §5.2.1)
//
// [v0.10.1 / R10-062] 本目录现在带一份 `wlwl.toml`,`gradual_typing = "error"`。
// 之前没有:默认档是 off,没有清单就没有 `[features]` 可读,所以这个旗舰示例
// **从不触发任何静态检查** —— 照着它学的人会以为注解是生效的。
//
// 想看 v0.9 的惰性行为(注解完全不参与运行),把这个文件单独拷到别处再跑。

// ── §5.2 annotations on a LET binding and on FUN parameters ────────────
LET(width: INTEGER, 3);
LET(area, FUN((w: INTEGER, h: INTEGER) : INTEGER, *(w, h)));
PRINT(width, area(2, 5));          // 3 10

// ── §5.2 container types ───────────────────────────────────────────────
LET(first, FUN((xs: ARRAY[INTEGER]) : INTEGER, INDEX_GET(xs, 0)));
PRINT(first([10, 20, 30]));        // 10

LET(lookup, FUN((d: DICT[STRING, INTEGER]) : INTEGER, AT_K(d, "k", -1)));
PRINT(lookup(["k": 42, "j": 7]));  // 42

// OPTION[T] is annotation sugar for RESULT[T, NULL] — there is no runtime
// OPTION type (spec §2.1). Both spellings are checked the same way.
LET(some, FUN((o: OPTION[INTEGER]) : BOOLEAN, IS_OK(o)));
PRINT(some(OK(1)));                // TRUE

LET(ok, FUN((r: RESULT[INTEGER, STRING]) : BOOLEAN, IS_OK(r)));
PRINT(ok(OK(1)));                  // TRUE

// ── §5.2.1 bounded type variables (erased at runtime) ──────────────────
// The constraint sits on a BARE IDENTIFIER. T is resolved at the call site
// against the actual argument types; the type variable itself disappears at
// runtime, so Value is unchanged.
// Named `pick_smaller` because that is what it does — `<` returns the LOWER
// operand. (There is no global MAX/MIN builtin; those live in `wlwl:std.math`
// since v0.11 and must be imported.)
LET(pick_smaller, FUN((a: T: Comparable, b: T: Comparable) : T: Comparable, IF(<(a, b), a, b)));
PRINT(pick_smaller(3, 9));              // 3
PRINT(pick_smaller("a", "b"));          // a

// ── Traps worth remembering (spec §5.2; behaviour measured on wlwl
//    0.11.0, 2026-10-01) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 1. ARRAY REQUIRES brackets: a bare ARRAY is E0010, but a bare DICT /
//    OPTION / RESULT parses as an opaque named type — silently, no error.
// 2. Angle-bracket and arrow forms are PARSE ERRORS (measured):
//        DICT<STRING, INTEGER>       -> E0011 expected ')', got Gt
//        FUN(INTEGER) -> STRING      -> E0012 expected ',', got Minus
//    Spec §5.2.1 still claims these parse silently into an opaque type
//    name. That sentence is STALE; the parser rejects both today.
// 3. A constraint may only follow a bare identifier. This is E0010, not a
//    no-op:
//        ARRAY[INTEGER]: Comparable  -> E0010
//    (Spec §5.2.1 says E0012 there; that code is return-type mismatch and
//    is unrelated. The implementation is the source of truth.)
